    notes: "WY added 2026-08-21, backlog item #6 from session 5's full-library audit (§11) — this one resolved to a genuine WY-specific finding, not an absence. Wyoming has its own assistance-animal-fraud misdemeanor statute (Wyo. Stat. § 35-13-207, enacted via 2017 House Bill 114, effective July 1 2017), punishable by a fine up to $750. Bill text pulled directly from wyoleg.gov (primary source) to confirm wording, corroborated by 5 independent secondary sources. Lives in Title 35, Chapter 13 — outside Title 1 entirely, so this is also a genuine 4th-gap-discovery-source find that the session-4 outside-Title-1 sweep missed. Structured parallel to assistance-animal-accommodation-co: same base text, WY-specific penalty citation substituted for CO's. Supersedes the generic assistance-animal-accommodation clause for WY. | PRIMARY-TEXT READ 2026-08-28 (Taylor supplied Wyo. Stat. 35-13-201 through 35-13-206 per 5a.2). MATERIAL CITATION CORRECTION: prior text cited '35-13-207', which DOES NOT EXIST (article ends at 35-13-206). Misrepresentation misdemeanor is 35-13-203(b). $750 figure CONFIRMED CORRECT and unchanged. Prior note claiming wyoleg.gov confirmation was wrong. SCOPE CONFIRMED: 35-13-203(b) reaches HOUSING - penalizes misrepresenting a service or assistance animal to obtain rights 'set forth in this article', and 35-13-201(c) is the residential-leasing right (unlike MN 609.833, which likely does not reach housing). ESA/HUD FEDERAL-CURRENCY QUESTION RESOLVED - INDEPENDENT STATE BASIS CONFIRMED: 35-13-201(c) independently bars discrimination in residential leasing 'because the person has an assistance animal'; 35-13-205(a)(iv) expressly includes an animal that 'provides emotional support that alleviates one or more identified symptoms or effects of a person's disability'. Stays VERIFIED, does NOT join KS/NE at NEEDS_REVIEW. QUALIFIER: 35-13-201(c) permits the animal 'in accordance with the federal Fair Housing Act', so mechanics are federally referenced; weaker than CO's CADA; no WY case law construes it. 2025 SF0147's $5,000 penalty is 35-13-206(a) (injuring/killing), a different offense.",
