    notes: "SD session 1. SDCL 43-32-24: 2-week (14-day) return/notice-of-withholding deadline runs from termination + receipt of tenant's forwarding address or delivery instructions (not from termination alone) - a shorter window than any state in this project so far (CO/WY/KS/NE/MN/ND all use 14-30+ days but none tie the clock to address receipt this explicitly at the 2-week mark). 45-day itemized-accounting-on-request deadline is separate and longer. Noncompliance = forfeiture of all withholding rights (matches ND's architecture) plus a separate punitive-damages exposure for bad-faith retention, capped at $200 (SDCL 43-32-24) - not included in lease-clause bodyText since it's a landlord-facing liability fact, not lease terms; see edu-security-deposit-itemized-accounting-sd. No deposit-interest requirement exists in SD (unlike MN/ND) - confirmed absent, not a product gap for this state. Primary source: SDCL 43-32-24, full text via consumer.sd.gov/docs/LLTen_Statutes43-32.pdf (SD Dept. of Labor & Regulation, Consumer Protection Division reproduction of the chapter), cross-checked against sdlegislature.gov's own section index (sdlegislature.gov/api/Statutes/43-32.html) for currency/completeness - section list matches exactly, no sections missing or renumbered. | CORRECTION 2026-09-07 (SD re-audit): shipped 'two weeks' as VERIFIED. SDCL 43-32-24 was AMENDED by SL 2026, ch 179, S 1 (2026 SB 4), effective July 1 2026, to TWENTY-ONE DAYS. Enacted text and source line (SL 1976 ch 267 S3; SL 1984 ch 281 S1; SL 2026 ch 179 S1) supplied by Taylor after two retrieval failures - escalated per S5a.2. Secondary sources split 2-2 at time of check, one carrying the old figure stamped 'Updated July 2026'. K.4 INVERTED: the stale text was TENANT-favourable (shorter deadline than law allows), so the extra-scrutiny-where-stale-text-is-landlord-favourable heuristic would NOT have caught it - see L.6. The 45-day accounting deadline, forfeiture rule and $200 punitive cap are unchanged and re-confirmed. TITLE NORMALISED 2026-09-19: 'Security Deposit Return (South Dakota)' -> 'Security Deposit Return' (state name in the title was a per-session convention used only by SD, OH, ND and CO).",
