    notes: "K.S.A. 31-162(c), Kansas Smoke Detector Act (K.S.A. 31-160 through 31-162). Full primary text read at ksrevisor.gov 2026-08-29. | NEW - closes a genuine gap. Kansas has had a statutory landlord smoke-detector duty since 1998 and the library carried ZERO KS rows on it through the original pass and every session since. | The install/maintain split is STATUTORY, not a drafting choice: 31-162(c) provides that the owner supplies and installs all required detectors and the owner tests and maintains them, EXCEPT inside rental units, where the occupant tests and maintains after taking possession. This clause mirrors that allocation rather than inventing one. | Found via gap-discovery source #4 (law outside the core act) during the named-topic canvass. The duty lives in Chapter 31 (Fire Protection), not the KRLTA - the same pattern as Nebraska's and North Dakota's smoke-detector duties. Third confirmation that a first pass confined to the core act's table of contents reliably misses real findings.",
