    notes: "MN added (MN re-audit 2026-09-03, canvass pass 2) — GAP FOUND, high value. Minn. Stat. §504B.182, read from revisor.mn.gov. MN had NO inspection row at all, while KS has move-in-inventory-ks and NE has edu-no-move-in-inventory-requirement-ne — MN was the only state with a real inspection statute and no row for it. ARCHITECTURE NOTE: MN's version is TENANT-REQUEST-TRIGGERED, not a mandatory joint signed inventory on a fixed timeline like Kansas's 5-day rule. What is mandatory is the LANDLORD'S NOTIFICATION of the option — at both ends of the tenancy. MN §13 correctly flagged this distinction ('don't conflate with KS's version') and then never built the row. Subd. 1(b)'s photo/video alternative requires TENANT AGREEMENT and written acknowledgment — it is not a unilateral landlord substitute. Waiver is void (subd. 4). See edu-inspection-notice-penalty-mn for the penalty, which is severe and attaches to the NOTICE failure, not just the inspection.",
