    notes: "MN added (MN re-audit 2026-09-03, canvass pass 2) — resolves the 'last-month's-rent deposit-application restriction' canvass topic for MN. Minn. Stat. §504B.178 subd. 8, read in full. KS has a comparable architecture per prior logs; MN had no row. NOTE THE EXCEPTIONS, which are easy to miss and run against the landlord: the restriction does NOT apply to an oral or written month-to-month tenancy where neither party has served a notice to quit, nor to the last month of a §559.21 contract-for-deed cancellation period or a chapter 580/581/582 foreclosure redemption period. A landlord asserting this against a month-to-month tenant with no notice to quit outstanding would be wrong. The penalty is deliberately stated in full because it is conditioned on the landlord having FIRST made written demand and given notice of the subdivision — without that step there is no penalty.",
