    notes: "MN added (MN re-audit 2026-09-03, canvass pass 2) — GENUINELY NEW TOPIC, not on the named-topic checklist for ANY state. Minn. Stat. §504B.118, read in full (single paragraph): 'A landlord receiving rent or other payments from a tenant in cash must provide a written receipt for payment immediately upon receipt if the payment is made in person, or within three business days if payment in cash is not made in person.' History: 2010 c 315 s 2. NO STATE in the library has a cash-receipt row — checked across all seven. RECOMMEND ADDING 'cash rent payment receipt duty' as a new named-topic checklist row for future states; it is the kind of small, absolute, easily-violated duty that produces disputes disproportionate to its size, and it applies to 'rent or other payments,' not rent alone. Note the interaction with edu-no-payment-method-fee-ban-mn: Minnesota does not ban cash payment or fee it, but does impose this receipting duty on it. GROUP NORMALISED 2026-09-19: 'Rent & Fees' -> 'Rent & Payment' (session drift; 12 canonical groups are used by all nine states).",
