    topicKey: "flag-display",
    notes: "OH: R.C. 5321.131, verified section-open 2026-09-18 (was UNVERIFIED on a chapter-level read). NEW TOPIC - no other state in this library has a flag-display row. (A) bars any rental-agreement restriction on the four flags. SCOPE CORRECTION from the first draft: the (B) notice-and-consultation duty applies ONLY to a flag POLE or a permanently affixed BRACKET, and only for the US and POW/MIA flags - it does not attach to the state flag or service flag limbs, and not to ordinary display. (B)(1)(a) requires discussion of local zoning and underground utility service requests (OUPS); (B)(1)(e) requires flag and pole size consistent with the size and character of the building. (C) SHIELDS THE LANDLORD: a landlord who does not receive the (B) notifications is not liable for damages, fines or costs arising from the tenant's placement of the pole or bracket. (D) any violating provision is unconscionable under 5321.14 and the violation is against public policy and unenforceable. (E) expressly preserves a lease covenant to return the premises in their original condition - carried into the clause text. LEGAL WATCH: SB 202 of the 136th GA would amend 5321.131 (and 4781.40); PASSED THE SENATE, NOT ENACTED as of 2026-09-18 - do not cite it, monitor it. TITLE NORMALISED 2026-09-19: 'Flag Display (Ohio)' -> 'Flag Display' (state name in the title was a per-session convention used only by SD, OH, ND and CO).",
