    contentType: "LEASE_CLAUSE",
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    effectiveFrom: "2018-01-01",
    lastChecked: "2026-09-19",
    topicKey: "immigration-status-inquiry",
    notes: "CA: Civ. Code s1940.3(b), primary text supplied by Taylor 2026-09-19 (AB 299, eff. 2018-01-01). THIS IS THE ACTUAL INQUIRY PROHIBITION - stronger and earlier in the process than ss1940.2(a)(5) and 1940.35, which the canvass row was answered with previously. s1940.3(b)(1) bars ANY INQUIRY at all; (b)(2) bars requiring disclosure or certification; (b)(3) bars disclosure for improper purposes. s1940.3(c)(2) is the landlord's safe harbour and the line the app must respect: requesting information to verify FINANCIAL QUALIFICATIONS or IDENTITY is permitted - so identity documents may be requested, status may not be asked about. A screening form asking for immigration status is unlawful on its face. s1940.05 separately defines 'immigration or citizenship status' to include a PERCEIVED status and association with someone perceived to have one, so the prohibition reaches assumptions, not just questions. s1940.3(a) also bars a PUBLIC ENTITY from compelling landlords to inquire or report - relevant if a local ordinance ever purports to.",
