    notes: "CA: Civ. Code s1941.3, read section-open 2026-09-19. A SEPARATE STATUTORY SECURITY DUTY the library had no row for in any state. s1941.3(a)(1): dead bolt extending at least 13/16 inch beyond the strike edge; horizontal sliding doors excluded; pre-existing half-inch bolts suffice until first repair or replacement after 1998-07-01. (a)(2) window devices, excluding louvered and casement windows and any window more than 12 feet vertically or 6 feet horizontally from ground, roof or platform. (a)(3) does not require installing a door or gate where none existed on 1998-01-01. s1941.3(b) is the allocation that makes this lease text: the TENANT must notify, and the landlord is NOT LIABLE unless it fails to correct within a reasonable time after actual or received notice - the same notice-shifting structure as the smoke alarm duty. s1941.3(c) gives the tenant the ss1942, 1942.4 and 1942.5 remedies, breach of contract, injunctive relief, AND an affirmative defence in an unlawful detainer after rent default with CCP s1174.2 relief - unusually broad. s1941.3(d): does not alter the landlord's general duty of care under s1714. s1941.3(f) exempts historically designated buildings. GROUP NORMALISED 2026-09-19: 'Property Condition' -> 'Landlord Responsibilities' (session drift; 12 canonical groups are used by all nine states).",
