    notes: "CA: Civ. Code ss1940.45, 1940.41, 1940.20 and 1940.10, read section-open 2026-09-19. Grouped because each is a 'landlord shall not prohibit' rule that a standard lease's general restrictions would otherwise silently breach - the same shape as the political-sign and waterbed findings on common-area-use. s1940.45 religious items: limits are a total display exceeding 36 by 12 square inches, obstruction of the door's operation, threat to health or safety, illegality, or obscenity. Applies to landlords, sublessors and HOAs alike. s1940.41 micromobility: the landlord may NOT ban ownership at all, and may ban in-unit storage and charging only by PROVIDING SECURE LONG-TERM STORAGE - defined at (a)(2) to require resident-only access, on-site location, protection from precipitation, one electrical connection per device, and NO CHARGE to tenants. Battery repair in the unit may be prohibited; changing a tyre or adjusting brakes may not. Disability accommodation overrides (c) and (b)(2)(C). s1940.10 personal agriculture applies only to property of NOT MORE THAN TWO UNITS; the landlord may approve container placement, prohibit synthetic chemicals, and require a written agreement on excess water and waste costs. s1940.10(f) and the clothesline rules both defer to s1954 for any inspection. GROUP NORMALISED 2026-09-19: 'Property Use' -> 'Rules & Regulations' (session drift; 12 canonical groups are used by all nine states).",
